  "end": 3.21
 },
 {
  "voice": "am_puck",
  "text": "Sound like you?",
  "start": 3.26,
  "end": 4.05
 },
 {
  "voice": "am_puck",
  "text": "This is Doug.",
  "start": 4.25,
  "end": 4.98
 },
 {
  "voice": "am_puck",
  "text": "Doug live in igloo.",
  "start": 5.03,
  "end": 5.94
 },
 {
  "voice": "am_puck",
  "text": "Igloo not Doug's.",
  "start": 6.01,
  "end": 6.89
 },
 {
  "voice": "am_puck",
  "text": "Igloo is Larry's.",
  "start": 6.94,
  "end": 7.8
 },
 {
  "voice": "am_puck",
  "text": "Larry is landlord. Larry own ten igloos.",
  "start": 7.85,
  "end": 10.1
 },
 {
  "voice": "am_puck",
  "text": "Every month, Doug pay Larry.",
  "start": 10.17,
  "end": 11.34
 },
 {
  "voice": "am_puck",
  "text": "One year. Nineteen thousand, two hundred dollars.",
  "start": 11.39,
  "end": 13.65
 },
 {
  "voice": "am_puck",
  "text": "Larry buy new hat.",
  "start": 13.72,
  "end": 14.63
 },
 {
  "voice": "am_puck",
  "text": "Doug make $3,200 a month.",
  "start": 14.73,
  "end": 17.17
 },
 {
  "voice": "am_puck",
  "text": "Rent is $1,600.",
  "start": 17.22,
  "end": 19.13
 },
 {
  "voice": "am_puck",
  "text": "That is half of Doug's money.",
  "start": 19.18,
  "end": 20.31
 },
 {
  "voice": "am_puck",
  "text": "Doug pay Larry. Then food. Then gas.",
  "start": 20.38,
  "end": 22.2
 },
 {
  "voice": "am_puck",
  "text": "Day 20. Doug have $200.",
  "start": 22.25,
  "end": 24.16
 },
 {
  "voice": "am_puck",
  "text": "Payday is in 10 days.",
  "start": 24.23,
  "end": 25.4
 },
 {
  "voice": "am_puck",
  "text": "Doug ask Larry: wait one week?",
  "start": 25.45,
  "end": 26.81
 },
 {
  "voice": "am_puck",
  "text": "Larry say: no.",
  "start": 26.86,
  "end": 27.64
 },
 {
  "voice": "am_puck",
  "text": "Doug look for cheaper igloo.",
  "start": 27.74,
  "end": 28.99
 },
 {
  "voice": "am_puck",
  "text": "Cheaper igloo is far away. Gas cost more.",
  "start": 29.04,
  "end": 31.28
 },
 {
  "voice": "am_puck",
  "text": "Doug eat snow.",
  "start": 31.35,
  "end": 32.08
 },
 {
  "voice": "am_puck",
  "text": "Doug poor.",
  "start": 32.13,
  "end": 32.74
 },
 {
  "voice": "am_puck",
  "text": "In real life, typical American rent is $1,962.",
  "start": 33.09,
  "end": 37.62
 },
 {
  "voice": "am_puck",
  "text": "That is $23,544 a year.",
  "start": 37.67,
  "end": 41.04
 },
 {
  "voice": "am_puck",
  "text": "Experts say: rent should be 30% of pay. Not 50%.",
  "start": 41.11,
  "end": 44.57
 },
 {
  "voice": "am_puck",
  "text": "About half of American renters pay more than 30%.",
  "start": 44.64,
  "end": 47.52
 },
 {
  "voice": "am_puck",
  "text": "That is 22.7 million families.",
  "start": 47.57,
  "end": 49.63
 },
 {
  "voice": "am_puck",
  "text": "And 12 million pay more than half.",
  "start": 49.7,
  "end": 51.19
 },
 {
  "voice": "am_puck",
  "text": "Doug rule: Take your pay. Multiply by 0.3.",
  "start": 51.39,
  "end": 54.03
 },
 {
  "voice": "am_puck",
  "text": "That is your max rent. For Doug, that is $960.",
  "start": 54.08,
  "end": 57.11
 },
 {
  "voice": "am_puck",
  "text": "Too high? Get a roommate. Two penguins, one igloo, half the rent.",
  "start": 57.18,
  "end": 60.06
 },
 {
  "voice": "am_puck",
  "text": "Save this.",
  "start": 60.21,
  "end": 60.84
 },
 {
  "voice": "am_puck",
  "text": "Comment your rent.",
  "start": 60.99,
  "end": 61.81
 },
 {
  "voice": "am_puck",
  "text": "Next time: Why Doug can't buy igloo?",
  "start": 61.86,
  "end": 63.54
 }
